{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Hypnotic Eye feels like a natural next choice after You Should Be So Lucky because I want to explore the Tom Petty and Benmont Tench connection.",
    "A Fool To Care connects directly to my interest in Memphis, while the Hendrix and blues-guitar suggestions fit the listening reflected in People, Hell & Angels and Old Sock."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shadows in the Night misses my current interest in blues and guitar-driven rock; traditional pop interpretations are not what I want today.",
    "Band of Brothers and Django and Jimmie lean toward country more than I want on this visit, and the Sons of Anarchy soundtrack is less appealing than a full album by an artist I follow."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interaction with Blown Away seems to have been taken as a broader desire for country albums than I currently have.",
    "An apparent overlap with roots-oriented music is not enough on its own: a tribute, soundtrack, or traditional-pop album can still feel distant from the specific artists and guitar sounds I want."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The direct artist connection from Memphis to A Fool To Care and the musical connection from You Should Be So Lucky to Hypnotic Eye matter most to my choices today.",
    "I rarely choose many items at once, so finding blues guitar or songwriting appealing does not mean I want it immediately; Hendrix, Born To Play Guitar, and the singer-songwriter suggestions can wait."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my blues and roots-rock interests, but my strongest choices follow specific artist connections rather than broad stylistic overlap."
}"}
